    "## 4. Regression to Mean Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "**Theory vs Experiment**: Split each player's career into two chronological halves. Theory predicts that extreme performers in the first half will regress toward the mean in the second half.\n",
    "\n",
    "We quantify:\n",
    "- Correlation between first-half and second-half performance\n",
    "- Slope of regression line (theory: slope < 1 indicates regression)\n",
    "- Individual regression magnitudes\n",
    "- Identification of overperformers and underperformers"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Initialize regression to mean analyzer\n",
    "regression = RegressionToMean(min_balls_per_half=100)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Theory vs Experiment analysis\n",
    "theory_exp = regression.theory_vs_experiment()\n",
    "\n",
    "print('=== Theory vs Experiment: Regression to Mean ===')\n",
    "print(f\"\\nTheory (sampling variation only):\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Estimated reliability: {theory_exp['estimated_reliability']:.4f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "t = theory_exp\n",
    "print(f\"\\nExperiment (actual data):\")\n",
    "summary = theory_exp['summary']\n",
    "print(f\"  Correlation: {t['correlation']:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  R-squared: {t['r_squared']:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  N players: {t['n_players']}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Mean regression magnitude: {t['mean_observed_regression']:.1f} points\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Slope: {summary['slope']:.4f} (slope < 1 indicates regression to mean)\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Players regressed: {summary['players_regressed']}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Players improved: {summary['players_improved']}\")"
   ]
  },
