    "## 5. Beta-Binomial Shrinkage (Empirical Bayes)\n",
    "\n",
    "Shrink observed rates toward league average using empirical Bayes. Applied to:\n",
    "- Strike rate (runs per ball)\n",
    "- Boundary rate (boundaries per ball)\n",
    "- Dismissal rate (disissions per ball)\n",
    "\n",
    "Method of moments and MLE for prior estimation. Players with small samples shrink more toward the prior."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Initialize shrinkage analyzer\n",
    "shrinkage = BetaBinomialShrinkage(min_balls=200)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Estimate prior using method of moments\n",
    "prior_mom = shrinkage.estimate_prior_moments()\n",
    "prior_mean_sr = prior_mom.alpha / (prior_mom.alpha + prior_mom.beta)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('=== Empirical Bayes Prior Estimates (Method of Moments) ===')\n",
    "print(f\"\\nBoundary Rate Prior:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  α = {prior_mom.alpha:.3f}, β = {prior_mom.beta:.3f}\")\n",
