    "## 6. Multiple Comparisons Correction\n",
    "\n",
    "When comparing many players, we must correct for multiple testing:\n",
    "- **Bonferroni**: Very conservative, controls FWER\n",
    "- **Holm-Bonferroni**: Step-down, more powerful FWER control\n",
    "- **Benjamini-Hochberg**: FDR control, standard for multiple testing\n",
    "- **Benjamini-Yekutieli**: FDR under arbitrary dependence\n",
    "\n",
    "Applied to: One player vs many others (e.g., Kohli vs 12 other top batters)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Initialize multiple comparisons\n",
    "mc = MultipleComparisons(alpha=0.05)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Compare Kohli vs other top batters\n",
    "comparison_players = [\n",
    "    'RG Sharma', 'CH Gayle', 'AB de Villiers', 'MS Dhoni',\n",
    "    'DA Warner', 'KL Rahul', 'S Dhawan', 'AM Rahane',\n",
    "    'JC Buttler', 'HH Pandya', 'Q de Kock', 'F du Plessis'\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "results = mc.player_comparison_correction('V Kohli', comparison_players, 'strike_rate', min_balls=10)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('=== V Kohli vs 12 Other Batters (Strike Rate) ===')\n",
    "print(f\"\\nComparison Results:\")\n",
    "for method in ['holm_bonferroni', 'benjamini_hochberg']:\n",
    "    m = results[method]\n",
    "    print(f\"\\n{m['method']}:\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  {m['n_rejected']}/{m['n_tests']} rejected\")\n",
    "    for r in m['results']:\n",
    "        status = 'SIGNIFICANT' if r['rejected'] else 'not significant'\n",
    "        print(f\"    {r['test']}: raw p={r['raw_p']:.4f}, corrected p={r['corrected_p']:.4f} ({status})\")"
   ]
